f) the corrective, time-bound measures being taken to improve traffic flow; and
g) whether any international traffic management standards or best practices are being
adopted to optimize road usage and ensure smooth and safe movement of vehicles?SAEED AHMAD MAITLA
Acting Secretary

Will the Minister for Interior and Narcotics Control be pleased to state:
a) the number of applications been submitted for repair/maintenance against houses
situated in Street No. 24 Sector G-6/2, Islamabad during last five years;
b) how many of those application have been entertained and carried out their work;
c) how many of those application are pending and their work to be carried out in future;
d) whether it is a fact that an application for repair/maintenance and white wash had been
submitted in the year 2023, Street No.24, Sector G-6/2, Islamabad but no action has been
taken in this regard; and
e) if answer to part (d) is in yes, reasons thereof with the time when said work wil be done?

Will the Minister for Finance and Revenue be pleased to state:
a) the legal framework currently governing the implementation of Capital Value Tax (CVT);
b) the year wise total amount of CVT assessed and collected during the last three Financial
Years thereof ;
c) the number of notices issued, orders passed and recovery proceedings initiated under the
relevant CVT, provisions during the last three years;
d) the number of appeals filed against CVT related orders, and their present status
(disposed of or pending); and
e) whether any amendments or policy reviews have been undertaken regarding CVT
implementation; if so, details thereof?

Will the Minister for Federal Education and Professional Training be pleased to state:
a) what is the current number of out-of-school children in Pakistan, province-wise;
b) what annual targets have been set out to reduce this figure;
c) what percentage of GDP is currently allocated to the education sector;
d) how does it compare with regional benchmarks;
e) whether any impact assessment has been conducted regarding the implementation of the
Single National Curriculum; if so, findings thereof; and
f) what is the student-to-teacher ratio in public schools across provinces and whether it meets
international standards?

Will the Minister for National Heritage and Culture Division be pleased to state:
a) whether recent restoration work at Taxila, including Mohra Moradu and Sirkap had
involved the use of cement in violation of accepted conservation standards; if so, details thereof;
b) whether the Government has taken notice of concerns raised by UNESCO regarding
improper conservation practices at Taxila;
c) if so, what corrective measures have been taken;
d) whether any independent technical audit has been conducted to assess the quality of
restoration work at Taxila; if not, reasons thereof;
e) what is the total budget allocated for the Taxila preservation projects and how much has
been utilized so far;
f) whether lack of expertise and coordination among relevant authorities has contributed to
unprofessional restoration practices;
g) if so, what accountability measures have been taken?

Will the Minister for Federal Education and Professional Training be pleased to state:
a) the prescribed criteria and procedure currently in place for the appointment of the Registrar in
the Federal Urdu University of Arts, Science and Technology;
b) whether these criteria were followed in letter and spirit in the appointment of the incumbent
Registrar;
c) the criteria and procedure actually adopted for the appointment of the incumbent Registrar;
d) whether the previous service record of the incumbent Registrar was taken into account before
his appointment, and if so, the details thereof;
e) whether it is correct that prior to his appointment, allegations of malpractice existed during his
service with previous employers, and if so, the details thereof;
f) whether any inquiry or investigation was conducted regarding such allegations and its outcome;
and
g) the steps taken or proposed to ensure transparency, merit, and corrective action in such
appointments?

Will the Minister for Finance and Revenue be pleased to state:
a) when was Medical and Conveyance Allowance of Federal Government employees last increased;
b) can a Government employee get any disease treated for the same amount of money;
c) does Government intends to increase these two allowances in the upcoming budget so that at
least Government employees are able to afford their treatment;
d) if no, the reasons thereof; and
e) if part (c) is yes, when and the details of increase to be made in aforesaid allowances?

Will the Minister In-Charge of the Establishment Division be pleased to state:
a) the nature of bank accounts maintained by the Federal Employees Benevolent and Group
Insurance Fund for disbursement of benefits under the various schemes;
b) whether such accounts are maintained in scheduled banks; if so, the justification thereof;
c) whether approval of the Ministry of Finance was obtained; if not, reasons thereof;
d) the total profit/interest earned during the last three years and its accounting treatments;
e) whether such earnings have been utilized for the benefit of employees; if so, details thereof; and
f) whether any audit objection or inquiry has been reported, and steps being taken to ensure
transparency and fix responsibility?

Will the Minister In-Charge of the Establishment Division be pleased to state:
a) whether a comprehensive scrutiny of assets of civil servants has been conducted during the last
five years; if so, the details thereof;
b) the modus operandi for such scrutiny, along with procedures for verification, cross-checking,
and monitoring of declared assets;
c) whether any discrepancies or irregularities were identified, including cases of assets held in the
name of others (benamidars), assets beyond known sources of income, or assets allegedly held
abroad;
d) if so, the details and action taken thereon;
e) whether it is a fact that there exists no effective mechanism for systematic verification of assets;
if so, the reasons thereof; and
f) what scientific, data-driven methods and international best practices are being adopted to detect
concealed or disproportionate assets and ensure transparency and accountability?

Will the Minister for Poverty Alleviation and Social Safety be pleased to state:
a) whether it is a fact that the fifty percent charity component is determined through a formula
approved in 2007, despite the absence of a clear definition of charity;
b) if so, how does Pakistan Bait-ul-Mal ensure equal opportunity, transparency and consistency in
evaluating all NGOs and prevent arbitrary or selective application of criteria;
c) whether there is a absence of independent third party oversight the internal evaluation process
of Pakistan Bait-ul-Mal includes any institutional safeguards, checks or audit mechanisms to prevent
bias, conflict of interest or manipulation in decision making; if so, the details thereof;
d) the comparative statement of findings and reasons of each NGOs approved and rejected for
financial assistance during the last six years;
e) whether rejected NGOs are given an opportunity to rectify deficiencies or submit additional
documents;
f) whether any formal right of appeal exists for aggrieved organizations;
g) if so, the details thereof including how many appeals were heard and decisions thereof?

Will the Minister for Industries and production be pleased to state:
a) the present administration and operational expenditure of Pakistan Steel Mills, including details of
budget allocated, released and actually utilized during the current and last financial year;
b) the outstanding dues of employees of the Mill including salaries, allowances and other benefits;
c) what activities or duties the employees are presently performing at the Mill; and
d) the total financial liabilities currently borne by the Mill including loans, bills and other obligations?

Will the Minister for Water Resources be pleased to state:
a) whether the Government has formulated any fee or "Water Pricing Policy", regarding the use of water;
b) whether this policy has been implemented uniform across the Industrial, Agricultural, and urban usage;
c) whether the revenue is generated from its utilization in water projects; and
d) if not, the details for government's planning for the financial protection of water resources?

Will the Minister for National Health Services, Regulations and Coordination be pleased to state:
a) whether the salary structure and allowances of employees of the Pakistan Nursing and Midwifery
Council are aligned with Federal Government pay scales and Rules;
b) if not, the grade-wise details of pay, allowances and percentages admissible, alongwith differences, legal
basis and justification thereof;
c) the names and designations of employees who have received additional/current charge payments during
the last three years, along with duration and amounts;
d) whether any employee has been granted salary/benefits of a higher grade than the substantive post,
including grant of orderly allowance to lower grades and if so, details thereof;
e) whether the Council is authorized to fix its own pay structure;
f) whether prior approval of the Ministry or Finance Division is required; and
g) the corrective measures are being taken or proposed in this regard?

Will the Minister for Railways be pleased to state:
a) the current status, scope, and key components of the Main Line-1 (ML-1) project, being a flagship
initiative for the development and modernization of Railway infrastructure;
b) the reasons for delay or failure to implement the project in recent years, including any financial,
administrative, or technical constraints;
c) whether any foreign investment, financing arrangements, or partnerships have been finalized or are
under consideration for the execution of ML-1; if so, the details thereof;
d) the estimated cost and revised timelines for completion of the project;
e) the concrete steps taken by the Government to operationalize and materialize ML-1 at the earliest; and
f) the measures being adopted to ensure transparency, efficiency, and timely execution of the project, along
with any matter ancillary or incidental thereto?

Will the Minister for Railways be pleased to state:
a) whether it is a fact that, prior to the recent Shalimar Express incident, an examination identified multiple
coaches with defective or non-functional braking systems; if so, the details thereof;
b) whether such coaches were cleared for operation despite these defects; if so, the reasons and officers
responsible;
c) whether the practice of deploying “dummy coaches” exists; if so, its extent, policy basis, and justification;
d) whether the inquiry into the incident has examined the role of maintenance, inspection, and supervisory
authorities in addition to the train crew; if so, the findings thereof;
e) what action has been taken against officials responsible for certifying unsafe rolling stock;
f) whether a system-wide audit of rolling stock has been conducted; if so, the
outcome thereof; and
g) the measures taken to ensure accountability, strengthen safety oversight, and prevent recurrence of such
incidents?

Will the Minister for Water Resources be pleased to state:
a) the year-wise details of total amount collected to date under the Prime Minister and Supreme Court
Diamer-Bhasha and Mohmand Dams Fund;
b) where the said funds are presently parked, including details of the banks, accounts, instruments, or
investments in which these funds are held;
c) whether the funds are being utilized for the construction of Diamer-Bhasha Dam and Mohmand
Dam; if so, the total expenditure incurred so far along with brief particulars;
d) whether any portion of the funds has been transferred, reallocated, diverted, or remains unutilized;
if so, the reasons thereof;
e) whether the fund has been subjected to audit; if so, the findings thereof; and
f) the measures taken to ensure transparency, accountability, and timely utilization of the funds, along
with any matter ancillary or incidental thereto?

Will the Minister for Railways be pleased to state:
a) whether it is a fact that quality and timeline violations were made in projects awarded to various
Railways contractors;
b) if so, the details of such projects and the action taken against the contractors responsible therefor;
c) whether any active blacklisting system is available; and
d) if not, the policy formulated to ensure transparent procurement and implementation?

Will the Minister for Maritime Affairs be pleased to state:
a) how many vessels have docked at each Pakistani Port during the last one year;
b) the month-wise details of these vessels, along with their cargo capacity and type at each port;
c) the total handling capacity of each port and its utilization during the said period;
d) whether it is a fact that certain ports are operating below optimal capacity; if so, the reasons thereof; and
e) what steps have been taken by the Government to improve port efficiency, reduce turnaround time, and
enhance competitiveness, particularly in view of regional competition and reported delays causing losses to the
national exchequer?

Will the Minister for Housing and Works be pleased to state:
a) the total number of members of all category who have applied in membership drive first come first serve
basis launched by Federal Government Employees Housing Authority (FGEHA), along with the details
thereof;
b) the details, as the number of plots alotted till March 2026 along with the list of the said plots thereof;
c) the list of members to whom plots have not been allotted so far;
d) the sectors in which plots will be allotted to those members to whom plots have not allotted so far; and
e) the time by which plots will be handed over to members?

Will the Minister for Housing and Works be pleased to state:
a) whether it is a fact that, in government residential colonies under the administrative control of the
Ministry, a private housing management company is collecting maintenance charges but has failed to provide
basic facilities;
b) whether, despite numerous complaints from the residents, no effective accountability mechanism has
been activated and also no action has been taken against the said company;
c) the reasons for not conducting an audit of the accounts and fees collected by the said company to date;
and
d) whether the Ministry intends to initiate any legal, regulatory, or administrative action against the said
management?

Will the Minister for Housing and Works be pleased to state:
a) whether it is a fact that a number of police officials who were serving as gunmen with
Ministers were performing duties in other departments and were allotted Government residences by
the Estate Office;
b) if so, the names, designations and house numbers of such officials;
c) whether the Estate Office has retrieved the houses after their retirement from the police
department; if not, the reasons thereof;
d) whether it is also a fact that some of the retired officials got the said houses allotted to their
children under Rule 15; and
e) if so, whether Rule 15 is applicable to such cases alongwith the details thereof?

Will the Minister for Railways be pleased to state:
a) whether it is a fact that Railways is suffering from a continuous annual budget deficit;
b) if so, the details of the subsidy, revenue and expenditures for the last five years;
c) whether any loan or assistance has been obtained from any financial institution or
international organization; and
d) if not, the details of Government's policy for achieving financial self-sufficiency?

Will the Minister for Communications be pleased to state:
a) whether any research or study has been conducted by the Ministry, National
Highways and Motorway Police (NHMP) any other affiliated agency, or through a
third party regarding the causes of accidents on National Highways and
Motorways;

b) if so, the details thereof, including categorized causes from major to minor;

c) if not, the reasons for not conducting such a study;

d) whether the Government plans to initiate a comprehensive exercise in this regard,
alongwith proposed timeline;

e) whether the government has taken notice of unauthorized, high-intensity or
modified vehicle lights that cause temporary blindness for oncoming drivers;
f) if so, their legal status, market availability, enforcement measures and the action
taken to control their use and sale;

g) whether capacity building of enforcement agencies is planned for effective
detection and regulation; and

h) the key outcomes expected from these efforts and the timeframe for achieving
them?

Will the Minister for Energy (Power Division) be pleased to state:
a) the total number of IPPs operating in the country alongwith detail of their ownership;
b) the volume of electricity being procured by the Government from these IPPs at present;
c) the total amount being paid to all IPPs at present; and
d) the amount being paid under the head of capacity payment?

Will the Minister for Science and Technology be pleased to state:
a) what percentage of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) is allocated to research and development (R and
D) in Pakistan;
b) how does it compare with neighboring countries;
c) how many patents have been registered in Pakistan over the last five years;
d) what steps are being taken to increase innovation output;
e) whether any national strategy exists to promote indigenous technological manufacturing; if
so, the details thereof; and
f) what is the current number of operational research laboratories and innovation centers
under the Ministry, and their performance indicators?

Will the Minister for Poverty Alleviation and Social Safety be
pleased to state;

(a) the details of the beneficiaries of different programs of
Benazir Income Support Programme (BISP) for Districts of
Lahore, Gujranwala, Jhang, Chiniot and Mandi Bahauddin;
and

(b) the details including names of beneficiaries during the last
three years;
